Article 1 (Purpose and Parties)
   These Terms set out the conditions for using the Colibre software (the "Software" or the "Service") and the rights and obligations of you (the "User") and the developer. The copyright holder and licensor of the Software is Lee BumSuk, an individual (the "Developer"). Business details are listed at the end of these Terms.
   By installing, copying or using the Software you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software. These Terms are the same as the license agreement shown on the installer screen; they are one agreement.

Article 2 (Nature of the Service)
   - The Software is a remote desktop Windows app that you install and run on your own PC. In the car’s web browser you see your own PC’s screen, and your phone works as the trackpad and keyboard. DRM-protected content on the remote desktop stays protected, and the Developer does not bypass it.
   - Connecting to, displaying and controlling your PC screen and handling files all happen only between your own PC and your own devices. The Developer and the Developer’s systems and facilities do not provide, hold, store, relay, cache, transmit or process your PC screen, media or files, and the Developer does not operate any service for that purpose.
   - Your car or phone connects directly to your PC using your own public IP address and certificate. No Developer system and no third-party intermediary sits on that path.
   - The Service works by having the car’s web browser connect to your PC and show your PC screen received over a mobile network (such as the car’s LTE); it is a remote desktop. Because of this design, (1) if the car’s browser clears its memory you may need to reopen the screen or reconnect, (2) screen updates and responses may be delayed depending on network conditions (especially car LTE), and (3) it may be slower or may stutter compared with using the PC directly. These are characteristics of how the Service is built. See "Good to know — characteristics and limits of the service" in the user manual for details.

