Article 12 (Keeping and Losing License Keys and Registration Numbers)
   - Your subscription is tied to the license key issued by the Payment Provider and works separately from the registration number (PIN, 15 digits). Losing the registration number does not end your subscription.
   - You cancel a subscription, check a license key or get a receipt through the Payment Provider using the email you bought with; a registration number is not needed (use the “Manage billing / cancel” link in Settings, which opens the Payment Provider’s customer portal).
   - A registration number is issued for each installed PC. The Developer cannot reissue or look it up for you.
   - If a phone you registered during setup is still signed in, you can view it again at the top of Settings.
   - Reissuing is allowed up to 5 times per day per installed PC, and the count resets at midnight Korea time.
   - A registered device (phone or car) can reissue from anywhere on an external network, including mobile data. An unregistered device can reissue at your home Wi-Fi or on the installed PC; away from home, a registered device (for example the car screen) must see the same 6-digit confirmation number and approve.
   - When you reissue, the old registration number and password become invalid immediately, and a notice appears on every device screen and on the installed PC.
   - If you lose a registered device, remove it from the device list right away.
   - The last resort when reissuing also fails is to choose "Delete settings too" when uninstalling the app and then reinstall. You get a new registration number and must set up devices and settings again from scratch. It is not guaranteed that your paid license carries over automatically. If the key is already linked to this PC, it may be rejected as "registered on another PC", so before uninstalling, use "Release this PC" under Settings > License first. If it is rejected, contact support from your purchase email.
   - When moving to another PC, release the license on the PC you were using ("Release this PC") before entering the key on the new PC (1 key = 1 PC).
   - You are responsible for keeping your license key, purchase email account, registration number and password safe. The Developer cannot reissue a license key or cancel a payment for you.
   - The Developer is not liable for damage caused by losing them, such as being unable to use the Service or the effort of resetting, unless there is intent or gross negligence. If a problem arises, contact the Developer’s support email (support@colibre.app).

